<title>NORWAY: BP spuds dry well off mid-Norway.</title>
<headline>BP spuds dry well off mid-Norway.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Norwegian Oil Directorate (OD) said on Thursday British Petroleum Norge had spudded a dry exploration well on block 6408/8, west of the Draugen field off mid-Norway.</p>
<p>The well was drilled to a depth of 1,937 metres under sea level.</p>
<p>BP was awarded operatorship of development licence 158 in Norway's 12th concession round in 1989 and holds 40 percent in the licence.</p>
<p>Other partners include Den norske stats oljeselskap AS with 50 percent and Norske Shell with 10 percent.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
